---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import DocumentDirectory from '../components/DocumentDirectory.astro';
const projects = [
{n:'01', category:'technical', type:'TECHNICAL WRITING', title:'OmniLib House documentation', description:'A complete documentation suite for OmniLib House — from architecture and API references to everyday user guides.', tags:['API documentation','User guides','Architecture'], href:'/work/technical-writing/readme', art:'docs', label:'OmniLib House', sub:'DOCUMENTATION THAT CONNECTS THE DOTS'},
{n:'02', category:'strategy', type:'DOCS-AS-CODE & STRATEGY', title:'Documentation strategy & workflows', description:'Scalable workflows, contribution guidelines, and content standards built for the way engineering teams work.',tags:['Docs-as-code','Content operations','Git'],href:'/work/docs-as-code/documentation-strategy',art:'flow',label:'From commit to clarity',sub:'A BETTER WAY TO BUILD DOCUMENTATION'},
{n:'03',category:'knowledge',type:'KNOWLEDGE MANAGEMENT',title:'Knowledge architecture & governance',description:'Information architecture, thoughtful taxonomies, and governance that turn scattered information into shared knowledge.',tags:['Information architecture','Taxonomy','Governance'],href:'/work/knowledge-management/knowledgebase-structure',art:'knowledge',label:'A place for every answer',sub:'ORGANIZE. CONNECT. DISCOVER.'},
{n:'04',category:'ai',type:'AI-ASSISTED DOCUMENTATION',title:'AI-assisted writing & review',description:'Practical approaches to AI-assisted writing, with purposeful prompts, structured reviews, and people at the center.',tags:['AI workflows','Prompt engineering','Content quality'],href:'/work/ai-assisted-documentation/workflow',art:'ai',label:'A thoughtful collaboration',sub:'HUMAN EXPERTISE × AI ASSISTANCE'}
];
---
<Layout title="Dhara Gohil — Technical Writer & Knowledge Strategist">
<section class="hero wrap">
<div class="hero-copy"><p class="eyebrow"><span class="status-dot"></span> TECHNICAL WRITER & KNOWLEDGE STRATEGIST</p><h1>Clear documentation.<br /><span>Confident users.</span></h1><p class="hero-description">I’m Dhara Gohil, a technical writer with a software development background. I create documentation and knowledge systems that help people understand and use technology.</p><div class="hero-actions"><a class="button" href="#documents">Browse documents <span>↗</span></a><a class="text-link" href="#about">About my experience <span>↓</span></a></div><div class="hero-note"><span class="tiny-line"></span> Developer roots. Writer’s perspective. Human-first thinking.</div></div>
<aside class="portfolio-overview" aria-label="Portfolio at a glance"><p class="eyebrow">AT A GLANCE</p><h2>Technology, explained<br />with people in mind.</h2><dl><div><dt>14+ years</dt><dd>Across technology & communication</dd></div><div><dt>9+ years</dt><dd>In technical writing</dd></div></dl><a href="#documents">Browse the document library <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></aside>
</section>
<div class="credentials"><div class="wrap"><span>14+ years across technology & communication</span><i>✳</i><span>Developer turned technical writer</span><i>✳</i><span>Clarity is always the goal</span></div></div>
<section class="document-library wrap" id="documents"><div class="section-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">BROWSE THE FULL COLLECTION</p><h2>Document library<span>.</span></h2></div><p>Choose a category, then open a writing sample.</p></div><DocumentDirectory /></section>
<section class="work wrap" id="work"><div class="section-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">A SELECTION OF WHAT I DO</p><h2>Selected work<span>.</span></h2></div><p>Start with these examples of my approach<br />to documentation and content strategy.</p></div><div class="filters" role="group" aria-label="Filter projects"><button class="active" data-filter="all" aria-pressed="true">All work <span>04</span></button><button data-filter="technical" aria-pressed="false">Technical writing</button><button data-filter="strategy" aria-pressed="false">Docs-as-code</button><button data-filter="knowledge" aria-pressed="false">Knowledge management</button><button data-filter="ai" aria-pressed="false">AI & documentation</button></div>
<div class="project-grid">{projects.map(p=><a class="project" href={p.href} data-category={p.category}><div class="project-meta"><span>{p.type}</span><span>↗</span></div><h3>{p.title}</h3><p>{p.description}</p><div class="tags">{p.tags.map(t=><span>{t}</span>)}</div></a>)}</div>
<div class="case-link"><span>Behind the documentation: the decisions, the process, the lessons.</span><a href="/work/case-studies/documentation-modernization">Explore a case study ↗</a></div></section>

<section class="expertise wrap" id="expertise"><div class="section-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">MY EVERYDAY TOOLKIT</p><h2>Expertise & tools<span>.</span></h2></div><p>The skills and tools behind<br />clear, useful content.</p></div><div class="expertise-list"><div><span>01</span><h3>Technical communication</h3><p>API references · User guides · Architecture documentation · Release notes</p></div><div><span>02</span><h3>Content & knowledge strategy</h3><p>Information architecture · Taxonomy · Content governance · Documentation strategy</p></div><div><span>03</span><h3>Tools & technologies</h3><p>DITA XML · Markdown · Git · Confluence · Oxygen XML · Visual Studio Code</p></div><div><span>04</span><h3>AI & modern workflows</h3><p>AI-assisted authoring · Prompt engineering · Agentic review · Docs-as-code</p></div></div></section>
<section class="about-section" id="about"><div class="wrap about"><div><p class="eyebrow">THE PERSON BEHIND THE WORDS</p><h2>From software development<br /><span>to technical writing.</span></h2></div><div class="about-copy"><p>I started in software development. Today, I help people understand the technology we build.</p><p>With 14+ years across technology and communication, including 9+ years in technical writing, I bring an engineer’s curiosity and a writer’s care to every project.</p><p>My work spans enterprise software, telecommunications, e-commerce, and industrial automation. Whether it’s an API reference or an entire knowledge ecosystem, I believe good documentation starts with understanding the person who needs it.</p><a class="text-link" href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/dhara-gohil-5630a254" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">More about my journey on LinkedIn ↗</a></div></div></section>

<section class="contact wrap" id="contact"><p class="eyebrow"><span class="status-dot"></span> OPEN TO THE NEXT CHAPTER</p><h2>Have something complex?<br />Let’s make it <em>clear.</em></h2><div><p>Let’s talk technical writing, knowledge strategy,<br />or your next documentation challenge.</p><a class="button" href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/dhara-gohil-5630a254" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Connect on LinkedIn ↗</a></div><span class="contact-star" aria-hidden="true">✳</span></section>
</Layout>
<script>
const buttons = document.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>('[data-filter]');
buttons.forEach(button => button.addEventListener('click', () => {
buttons.forEach(item => { item.classList.toggle('active', item === button); item.setAttribute('aria-pressed', String(item === button)); });
document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-category]').forEach(project => { project.hidden = button.dataset.filter !== 'all' && project.dataset.category !== button.dataset.filter; });
}));
</script>
